Darwin: a batch's two job chains in one kernel request, in a Metal process.

A34 (local to this port; nothing here goes upstream). Kernel 0988's SUBMIT_BATCH (request 0x7d)
queues several SUBMITs at once; redwood-drm's redwood_drm_submit_batch (userland/mesa/redwood-drm)
sends them and answers their syncobjs. In a process drawing through Metal (redwood_pan_metal),
jm_submit_batch sends a batch's vertex/tiler chain and its fragment job together instead of one
request each: ~35 us a request, two a batch, ~15 batches a frame (boot 0980-b). Both jobs name
the same buffers, gathered once. When the kernel or the mode has no SUBMIT_BATCH (ENOTSUP,
nothing queued), and with in-syncs, tracing or no-op contexts, the two go one by one as upstream.

